- 2023ApJ...950...75I: When HCO+ column density and HCN-to-HCO+ abundance ratio are very high, HCN becomes optically thick and its flux saturates, so derived N_HCO+ and [HCN]/[HCO+] values can be lower limits
- 2023ApJ...950...75I: In the Bayesian MCMC analysis, the number of independent line ratios (5) is smaller than the total number of free parameters including flux scaling factors (7), and three ULIRGs (IRAS 15250+3609, Sup…
- 2016Natur.537..207G: Temperature uncertain due to lack of high-J CO lines at high resolution; magnetic fields need observational confirmation
- 2018A&A...610A..77H: HiFIVE fails on the most complex structures (fibers 21, 36/37, 42/43); the 55 fibers are a simplified description
- 2018A&A...610A..77H: Mass conversion uncertain by factor 2-3; lengths not corrected for projection
- 2020ApJ...902...99I: Emission larger than the maximum recoverable scale may be resolved out
- 2020ApJ...902...99I: Extended host-galaxy emission is not recovered in the Cycle 6 data, so only compact torus emission is discussed
- 2020ApJ...902...99I: Continuum peak flux uncertainties exclude absolute flux calibration and continuum frequency-range choice
- 2020ApJ...902...99I: C-peak spectra can be contaminated by innermost torus emission because the beam is not much smaller than the separation
- 2020ApJ...902...99I: HCO+-VIB emission candidate is below 3 sigma and may be HOC+
- 2021A&A...648A..38G: The sample of sight lines used for n(H)/G0 includes CO and HCO+ detections, which may bias densities high
- 2021A&A...648A..38G: Aspects of the C+ + H2O reaction (rate, branching ratio) may not be fully understood, so the HOC+ comparison is uncertain
- 2024ApJ...969..102N: Archival calibrator data have poorer angular resolution, frequency resolution and sensitivity than the dedicated CO data
- 2024ApJ...969..102N: Some components heavily contaminated by other lines were excluded for CN, HCN and C2H
- 2024ApJ...969..102N: Narrower line components may exist but SNR prevents identification
- 2024ApJ...969..102N: H2CO only marginally detected because of limited sensitivity
- 2024ApJ...969..102N: Atomic carbon results limited by archive SNR
- 2024ApJ...969..102N: N(H2) from 13CO emission in diffuse gas is highly uncertain and often severely underestimated
- 2025ApJ...985..259J: In-band mm spectral index poorly constrained due to low sensitivity and limited bandwidth
- 2025ApJ...985..259J: IRAS 25/60 micron comparison cannot be made fairly because of sample selection bias
- 2025ApJ...985..259J: Heavily Compton-thick AGN (NH > 1e25) are largely absent, so CONs as an extreme CT subset are not excluded
- 2025ApJ...985..259J: Origin of the molecular outflows (AGN vs starburst) is unclear, e.g. NGC 6240
- 2017ApJ...850..170O: Differential magnification is a main uncertainty
- 2017ApJ...850..170O: Scatter and lack of homogeneous high-z samples prevent redshift trends
- 2013A&A...555A.112P: Dust opacity, temperature uncertainties; 1D model cannot describe filaments
- 2019ApJ...883..193N: Missing flux from lack of short baselines, so masses are lower limits
- 2019ApJ...883..193N: Residual is not a true chi2 because neighbouring pixels are correlated; modelling assumptions simple
- 2023A&A...679A.119R: Low S/N of HCO+(4-3) precludes reliable assessment of its spatial morphology and precludes source-plane reconstruction.
