- 2023A&A...679A.119R: Sub-solar metallicity in SDP.81 might not be representative of the general DSFG population.
- 2026ApJ..1000..141K: The Band 3 and Band 4 observations were separated by ~9 months (October 2016 to July 2017) without simultaneous millimeter monitoring, though a few percent variability would shift T_CMB by < 0.1 K.
- 2026ApJ..1000..141K: The -6 km/s component cannot constrain f_c due to lack of saturation, leaving its T_ex uncertain.
- 2026ApJ..1000..141K: H13CN and H13CO+ transitions have low S/N (~3), limiting their statistical significance.
- 2014ApJ...795...28B: Mass-loss rate is poorly constrained; density is an upper bound, column a lower bound, layer thickness unknown
- 2025A&A...699A..17L: All directions in the Galactic anticenter were observed for the same integration time, resulting in strongly varying rms line-to-continuum sensitivities depending on background source flux.
- 2025A&A...699A..17L: The sample is an inhomogeneous amalgamation of datasets taken over 30 years with different selection criteria and is biased toward higher reddening and molecular gas content than the Galactic average.
- 2025A&A...699A..17L: Integration times were too short to provide useful upper limits on CS chemistry at E_B-V <= 0.5 mag.
- 2025A&A...699A..17L: Weak broad absorption components introduce ambiguities when matching Gaussian components across species.
- 2025A&A...699A..17L: Averaged CO and HCO+ emission spectra were derived over slightly different spatial regions offset from the pencil-beam absorption sight line.
- 2022RAA....22f5021G: Large uncertainty in the rate constant for the radiative association reaction C6H5 + OH -> C6H5OH + hnu (reaction 5), which has not been previously studied for phenol.
- 2022RAA....22f5021G: Low-temperature ice-phase hydrogen abstraction reactions (below 20 K) fall outside the temperature limits prescribed by combustion/high-temperature literature.
- 2022RAA....22f5021G: DFT-B3LYP/6-31G(d,p) calculations of enthalpy of formation show a large deviation from experimental values compared to the G4 composite method.
- 2022RAA....22f5021G: Expected antenna temperature comparisons (mu_total^2 / Q_rot) do not account for molecular abundances, which are controlled by kinetic reaction pathways.
- 2014ApJ...785..149S: Single-component modelling of a heterogeneous sample; no single model fits (chi2 min 10.4 for 3 dof); degeneracies remain; differential magnification not accounted
- 2026MNRAS.549ag931B: HCN(4-3), HCO+(4-3), 13CO(4-3), and C18O(4-3) were not detected in the Band 2 data.
- 2026MNRAS.549ag931B: Large uncertainties on individual dense gas line fluxes and compounding errors in their ratios limit constraints on HCN, HNC, and HCO+ line ratios.
- 2026MNRAS.549ag931B: Determining whether the clumps are rotationally supported fragments of a turbulent disc or the product of a recent merger requires future high-resolution CO and [C II] observations.
- 2014A&A...569L...5M: Uncertainty in v_LSR due to complex Orion kinematics
- 2018ApJ...856..143I: Only two J-transitions, so RADEX needs an assumed column density
- 2018ApJ...856..143I: Outflow N(H2) is a lower limit, and starburst galaxies lack isotopologue data
- 2025A&A...693A.199C: Beam-filling assumption may fail at Shock and cannot be tested for the additional transitions/species
- 2025A&A...693A.199C: MIREX fails at bright Mid-IR sources and can underestimate masses
- 2025A&A...693A.199C: Ambient may also be shock affected within the large single-dish beam
- 2025A&A...693A.199C: Magnetic support is unresolved; the existing G034.77 field estimate is indirect and uncertain
- 2025A&A...693A.199C: Higher-resolution 1 mm data needed to establish continuum counterparts
- 2025A&A...693A.199C: ALMA field does not cover the previously reported star-forming region near the HII region
- 2025A&A...693A.199C: Shock-triggering scenario and core nature require additional observations
- 2020ApJ...902..140N: Only one HCO+ transition, so Tex could not be derived from the data and was assumed
- 2020ApJ...902..140N: Spatial resolution limits the smallest clump sizes that can be resolved
- 2020ApJ...902..140N: M_LTE may be underestimated, and optical depth may be underestimated because of a small beam filling factor
- 2014A&A...570A..28V: RADEX assumes all transitions sample the same gas, and several ratios use degraded or low-resolution data
- 2014A&A...570A..28V: Chemical modelling is preliminary and compares time-dependent models only at one time step
- 2014A&A...570A..28V: Infrared pumping not considered
- 2024ApJ...977...38B: Initial chemical conditions may affect phase-2 starting abundances; varying them requires rebuilding the training set.
- 2024ApJ...977...38B: The emulator may smooth posterior structure; finer-grid testing remains necessary.
- 2024ApJ...977...38B: Kinetic temperature is poorly constrained.
- 2024ApJ...977...38B: The chemical framework is unsuitable for UV-dominated or shocked regions.
- 2024ApJ...977...38B: The emulator can extrapolate below the chemical grid's reliable abundance threshold.
- 2024ApJ...977...38B: Larger regions mix diffuse and dense gas and complicate comparison with previous GMC measurements.
- 2024ApJ...977...38B: SpectralRadex performs poorly at unrealistically high molecular column densities.
- 2024ApJ...977...38B: The timing of observable cosmic-ray suppression of star formation is uncertain.
- 2023ApJ...942...25F: Inferred density and temperature from RADEX are highly degenerate when only J <= 3 CO lines are sampled and cannot rule out a secondary warm/hot molecular gas component.
- 2023ApJ...942...25F: Combining single-dish IRAM 30m and interferometric ALMA measurements introduces ~37% flux uncertainty.
- 2023ApJ...942...25F: More than 50% of the CO (3-2) flux in H02 and H03 is contained within a central unresolved beam.
- 2023ApJ...942...25F: The rapid early decline in L'_HCO+/L'_CO with post-burst age is driven by a single young galaxy (R02), requiring a larger sample to confirm.
- 2023ApJ...942...25F: Cannot fully rule out an obscured nuclear starburst (SFR ~ 5 M_sun yr^-1) in H02 and H03 where TIR SFRs strongly exceed Halpha SFRs and mid-IR Neon spectroscopy is unavailable.
- 2018A&A...610A..49L: HI spin temperature result limited by noise in old HI absorption profile and spans dark to diffuse gas temperatures
- 2019A&A...632A..83S: CMF uncertain due to low-number statistics and 3.1 mm dust emissivity; free-free contamination in continuum
- 2022A&A...667A.131B: Not all sub-regions have been observed at all spatial resolutions for all molecules; NSB-b lacks consistent resolution observations and NSB-c has only a single high-resolution ratio (with HCN(4-3) an…
- 2022A&A...667A.131B: Gas kinetic temperature, gas density (except in E Knot, W Knot, and NSB-a at 40 pc), and linewidth are poorly constrained by the MCMC RADEX fitting across resolutions.
- 2022A&A...667A.131B: Follow-up studies of other nearby galaxies are required to confirm whether HCN(4-3)/HCO+(4-3) and HCN(4-3)/CS(2-1) hold as reliable diagnostics beyond NGC 1068.
- 2020NatAs...4.1064H: Observational density and velocity estimators can alter inferred structure functions.
- 2020NatAs...4.1064H: Mock-field tests lack physical excitation and optical-depth treatment.
- 2020NatAs...4.1064H: Randomly generated periodicity does not establish a physical origin.
- 2020NatAs...4.1064H: Simple cylindrical fragmentation omits shear and magnetic fields.
- 2020NatAs...4.1064H: Exact GMC scaling exponents require caution because centroids convolve density, velocity and excitation.
- 2020NatAs...4.1064H: Directional anisotropy in the CMZ GMC is tentative and needs further investigation.
- 2024A&A...690A.372L: Gradient depends on the accuracy of kinematic-distance-based R_GC
- 2024A&A...690A.372L: Limited R_GC range of the sample
- 2024A&A...690A.372L: Pure circular motions may fail near the GC
- 2025A&A...702A.183H: Lacking spectroscopic redshifts and relative velocities for the secondary submm counterparts, it is impossible to confirm individual pairs as physical associations or true mergers.
- 2025A&A...702A.183H: SDSS optical imaging has insufficient spatial resolution and sensitivity to detect morphological signs of recent merger activity such as tidal tails, and post-coalescence mergers or line-of-sight com…
- 2025A&A...702A.183H: FIR selection inherently biases the sample towards gas- and dust-rich systems that are more likely to be involved in mergers compared to optically selected quasars.
- 2025A&A...702A.183H: Sensitivity for CO transitions with J_upp >= 11 is <= 5 sigma, preventing firm conclusions on those very high-J lines, and the small number of expected mid-J CO transitions limits statistical compari…
- 2018A&A...620A.115B: Low S/N; conversion 5-4 to 4-3 uncertain; differential lensing neglected
- 2014ApJ...793...37A: Marginally resolved clumps have large radius uncertainties; only 4 of 13 clumps deconvolved.
- 2017ApJ...843..136E: Missing short spacings: ~50% flux lost in CO(3-2); extended emission affected
- 2021A&A...645A..45C: Strong parameter degeneracies in LVG models
- 2025ApJ...993..134K: Time variability and covering factors in multiple subcomponents of the HCN spectra cannot yet be quantified directly

