## Paper excerpts (40 of 180, chosen for detail and spread over fields/years)

### 2018ApJ...868L..38G: Do Spectroscopic Dense Gas Fractions Track Molecular Cloud Surface Densities? (2018; nearby_galaxies, star_formation, milky_way_ism; archival_reuse)
- question: Does the spectroscopic dense gas fraction (HCN/CO) correlate with the cloud-scale (120 pc) molecular gas surface density in nearby galaxies?
- step 1: Measure HCN/CO at common resolution
  - method: Convolve HCN and CO(1-0) to common physical resolution; integrate HCN with CO-based PPV mask; ratio of integrated intensities [2.1 HCN (1-0) to CO (1-0) Ratio: "At this common resolution, we measure HCN/CO, the ratio of the HCN(1-0) to CO(1-0) integrated intensities."]
  - software: CASA
  - parameter: 650 pc (ALMA), 2770 pc (EMPIRE) [2.1 HCN (1-0) to CO (1-0) Ratio: "This is 650 pc for ALMA and 2770 pc for EMPIRE."]
  - validation: Compared ALMA and EMPIRE HCN/CO and different CO(1-0) sources for NGC 4321 [2.5 Additional Checks: "The ALMA and EMPIRE results agree within $0.06$ dex."]
- step 2: Compute intensity-weighted cloud-scale CO(2-1) intensity per HCN beam
  - method: Convolve CO(2-1) at 120 pc, calculate <I> = (I^2 * Omega)/(I * Omega) with Gaussian kernel [2.2 Average Cloud-Scale CO Intensity in…: "we calculate the intensity-weighted average $I_{\rm CO(2-1)}$ within each larger HCN beam."]
  - parameter: 120 pc resolution; PAWS CO(1-0) scaled by 0.7 for NGC 5194 [2.2 Average Cloud-Scale CO Intensity in…: "We convolve all four CO (2-1) maps to share this common physical resolution."]
  - assumption: alpha_CO(2-1) ~ 6.2 Msun pc-2 (K km/s)-1 (Galactic, with CO(2-1)/(1-0)=0.7) [2.4 Interpretation in Terms of Physical…: "the Galactic CO-to-H$_2$ conversion factor is $\alpha_{\rm CO (2-1)} \approx 6.2$ M$_\odot$ pc$^{-2}$ (K km s$^{-1}$)$^{-1}$."]
  - validation: Monte Carlo with 100 noise realizations gives ~2 K km/s mean error [2.2 Average Cloud-Scale CO Intensity in…: "We repeat this process 100 times, and calculate the standard deviation in $\left< I_{\rm CO(2-1)} \right>$ over all realizations."]
- step 3: Bin HCN/CO by <I_CO(2-1)>
  - method: Average integrated HCN divided by integrated CO in bins of <I_CO(2-1)> [2.3 Binned Relation: "we measure the average HCN/CO in bins of $\left< I_{CO (2-1)} \right>$."]
  - validation: Spectral stacking agrees with mask-and-average within ~10% [2.3 Binned Relation: "the spectral stacking yields the same results as our mask-and-average approach within ${\sim}10$%, with no systematic offset."]
- step 4: Quantify correlation and fit power law
  - method: Spearman rank correlation and bisector linear fit in log-log [3.1 Observed Correlation Between HCN/CO…: "Table [2](#tab:results) reports power law fits (fit via the bisector method)"]
  - assumption: alpha_CO(1-0)=4.35, alpha_HCN~14 for f_dense; f_dense ~ 2.3 HCN/CO [2.4 Interpretation in Terms of Physical…: "we assume $\alpha_{\rm CO (1-0)} = 4.35$ M$_\odot$ pc$^{-2}$ (K km s$^{-1}$)$^{-1}$ (cite: BOLATTO13)"]
  - fitting: bisector linear fit to log data [Observed Correlation Between HCN/CO and…: "Table [2](#tab:results) reports power law fits (fit via the bisector method) that offer a reasonable description of each sample."]
- result: Spearman rank correlation, ALMA 650 pc = 0.83 ± not stated dimensionless [Table 2: "| ALMA | 650 pc | $0.83$ | $0.81 (\pm 0.09), -1.93 (\pm 0.04)$ |"]
- result: Power-law slope, ALMA 650 pc = 0.81 ± ±0.09 dimensionless [Table 2: "| ALMA | 650 pc | $0.83$ | $0.81 (\pm 0.09), -1.93 (\pm 0.04)$ |"]
- result: Power-law slope, ALMA 2770 pc = 0.41 ± ±0.04 dimensionless [Table 2: "| ALMA | 2770 pc | $0.77$ | $0.41 (\pm0.04), -1.73 (\pm 0.02$) |"]
- result: Power-law slope, EMPIRE 2770 pc = 0.55 ± ±0.05 dimensionless [Table 2: "| EMPIRE | 2770 pc | $0.78$ | $0.55 (\pm0.05), -1.73 (\pm 0.01)$ |"]
- result: Scatter in HCN/CO at fixed <I_CO> = 0.11 (ALMA), 0.08 (EMPIRE) ± not stated dex [3.1 Observed Correlation Between HCN/CO…: "The standard deviation in HCN/CO at fixed $\left< I_{\rm CO(2-1)} \right>$ is 0.11 dex for the ALMA sample and 0.08 dex for the EMPIRE sample."]
- result: Intensity-weighted vs unweighted average offset = 0.6 dex at 650 pc; 1.4 dex at 2770 pc ± not stated dex [2.2 Average Cloud-Scale CO Intensity in…: "is $0.6$ dex higher at 650 pc resolution and $1.4$ dex higher at 2770 pc resolution."]
- limitation (authors): HCN-to-dense-gas conversion and effective critical density remain uncertain [2.4 Interpretation in Terms of Physical…: "Both the density of gas traced by HCN (1-0) and the conversion from HCN emission to a dense gas mass remain uncertain."]
- limitation (authors): Distances uncertain by 10-30% [2.2 Average Cloud-Scale CO Intensity in…: "The distances to our targets are uncertain by $\sim 10{-}30\%$."]
- not stated (card): ALMA HCN imaging details: robust, taper size, cell size, CASA version; Exact bin edges/widths in <I_CO(2-1)> and number of bins; Bisector fit implementation details; Intensity thresholds for CO mask and detection; Model density thresholds (n_eff) values used for models; Calibrator and flux scale details

### 2026A&A...711A.239S: ALMA-IMF: XXI. N<SUB>2</SUB>H<SUP>+</SUP> kinematics in the G012.80 protocluster: Evidence of filament rotation and evolution (2026; star_formation, milky_way_ism; large_program_or_survey)
- question: Characterize dense gas kinematic processes, line-mass profiles, and evolutionary stages of the two main filaments (R1 and R2) in the G012.80 massive protocluster using N2H+(1-0) and complementary lines.
- step 1: Data preparation, continuum subtraction, feathering, and S/N masking
  - method: Clean N2H+(1-0) observations with the ALMA-IMF pipeline, subtract continuum using imcontsub in emission-free channels, combine 7m, 12m, and TP data using feather, and construct pixel-by-pixel S/N maps from emission-free RMS noise. [ALMA-IMF datacubes: "We use the `imcontsub` task to subtract the continuum emission from the N$_2$H$^+$ line emission. To estimate the continuum emission we consider only emission-free channels, in the range of 12 to 20 $\rm km\,s^{-1}$, where we apply a linear fit using `fitorder` = 0."] [ALMA-IMF datacubes: "To recover the cloud emission at all available scales, we combine observations of the 7m and 12m arrays with total power data (TP). For this, we use the `feather` task."]
  - software: CASA, imcontsub, feather, ALMA-IMF imaging pipeline
  - parameter: fitorder = 0 in channels 12 to 20 km s^-1 for imcontsub [ALMA-IMF datacubes: "To estimate the continuum emission we consider only emission-free channels, in the range of 12 to 20 $\rm km\,s^{-1}$, where we apply a linear fit using `fitorder` = 0."]
