### 2013PASJ...65..100I: Submillimeter ALMA Observations of the Dense Gas in the Low-Luminosity Type-1 Active Nucleus of NGC1097 (2013; nearby_galaxies, astrochemistry, agn_and_quasars; observational_alma_primary)
- question: What are the characteristics of the dense gas around the low-luminosity type-1 AGN of NGC 1097, and what mechanism causes the HCN enhancement?
- step 3: Make moment maps and extract line fluxes
  - method: Zeroth moment using channels >3 sigma; first and second moments with 5 sigma clipping; integrated intensities from moment-0 at continuum peak; upper limits assuming Gaussian with FWHM like HCN [4 Channel maps and integrated intensiti…: "we computed these moment maps by using channels which contain $>$ 3 $\sigma$ emission only"] [5 Band 7 spectra: "Upper limits to the integrated intensities were derived for these undetected transitions assuming a Gaussian profile with FWHM similar to the $\Delta$$v$ derived for HCN ($J$ = 4–3)."]
  - software: MIRIAD MOMENT
  - parameter: 1 sigma = 2.27 mJy/beam (HCN), 2.39 mJy/beam (HCO+) [4 Channel maps and integrated intensiti…: "where 1 $\sigma$ = 2.27 mJy beam$^{-1}$ for HCN ($J$ = 4–3) and 2.39 mJy beam$^{-1}$ for HCO$^+$ ($J$ = 4–3)"]
- step 5: LTE rotation diagram analysis
  - method: Optically thin LTE excitation diagrams of HCN and HCO+ with J=1-0, 3-2, 4-3 convolved to common beam; single and two-component fits [8.1 Column density under LTE: "we estimate the rotational temperatures ($T_{\rm{rot}}$) and column densities ($N_{\rm{mol}}$) of HCN and HCO$^+$ molecules in the nuclear region via excitation diagrams (rotation diagrams)."]
  - parameter: common beam 4.4 x 2.7 arcsec, P.A. -14.6 deg [8.1 Column density under LTE: "We convolved all maps to 4$''$.4 $\times$ 2$''$.7 with P.A. = -14.6$^\circ$"]
  - assumption: Optically thin, LTE; T_rot lower limit to T_kin [8.1 Column density under LTE: "the derived $T_{\rm{rot}}$ is thus only a lower limit to the kinetic temperature"]
  - fitting: linear fit of log(N_u/g_u) vs E_u [Column density under LTE: "Therefore, the decimal logarithm of $N_u/g_u$ versus $E_u/k_{\rm B}$ will yield a straight line with a slope of $-\log{e}/T_{\rm{ex}}$."]
  - validation: Compared to ring, NGC 253, NGC 1068 [8.1 Column density under LTE: "we also made excitation diagrams of HCN and HCO$^+$ in one position in the circumnuclear starburst ring of NGC 1097"]
- step 6: Non-LTE RADEX chi2 grid
  - method: RADEX grid in T_kin, n_H2, N_HCO+/dV, [HCN]/[HCO+]; chi2 on line-ratio constraints; final use of high-J ratios R43/43 and R32/32 [8.2 Non-LTE excitation analysis: "we ran RADEX for each ($N_{\rm {HCO^+}}$/$dV$, \[HCN\]/\[HCO$^+$\]) case by changing $n_{\rm H_2}$ and $T_{\rm {kin}}$, and carried out a $\chi^2$ test"]
  - software: RADEX, LAMDA
  - parameter: T_kin 10–600 K in 10 K steps; n_H2 10^2–10^7 cm^-3 in steps x10^0.25; dV = 250 km/s; T_bg = 2.73 K; N_H2 = 4.8e22 cm^-2 representative [8.2 Non-LTE excitation analysis: "we varied the gas kinetic temperature within a range of $T_{\rm{kin}}$ = 10 – 600 K using steps of $dT_{\rm{kin}}$ = +10 K"]
  - assumption: Spherical geometry, homogeneous single-component medium; [HCO+]/[H2]=5e-9 [8.2 Non-LTE excitation analysis: "RADEX uses an escape probability approximation to solve the non-LTE excitation in a homogeneous (single temperature, single density), single component medium"]
  - fitting: chi2 grid search; well-fitted defined as chi2 <= 0.1 [8.2 Non-LTE excitation analysis: "Within the range of well fitted cases (we define as $\chi^2$ $\leq$ 0.1)"]
  - validation: Low-J vs high-J inconsistent fit (chi2 = 7.774) motivates using only high-J [8.2 Non-LTE excitation analysis: "$\chi^2$ = 7.774), from which we consider the $\chi^2$ value is too high"]
- result: HCN J=4-3 integrated intensity at peak = 7.5 ± 0.1 Jy/beam km/s [Table 3: "| HCN ($J$ = 4–3) | 354.505 | 42.5 | 38.8$\pm$2.3 | 199$\pm$8.3 | 7.5$\pm$0.1 | 40.5$\pm$0.5 |"]
