- result: R_HCNv/HCN upper limit = <0.08 ± not stated dimensionless [abstract: "The upper limit of the brightness temperature ratio of HCN ($v_2$ = 1$^{1f}$, $J$ = 4–3) to HCN ($J$ = 4–3) is 0.08"]
- result: R_HCN/CS lower limit = >12.7 ± not stated dimensionless [abstract: "which is more than 12.7 on the brightness temperature scale"]
- result: T_rot(HCN), single component = 7.76 ± 0.26 K [Table 8: "| $T_{\rm{rot}}$(HCN) \[K\] | 7.76$\pm$0.26 |"]
- result: N_HCN/N_HCO+ (nucleus) = 3.45 ± 0.60 dimensionless [Table 8: "| $N_{\rm{HCN}}/N_{\rm{HCO^+}}$ | 3.45$\pm$0.60 |"]
- result: Non-LTE [HCN]/[HCO+] range = 5–20 ± not stated dimensionless [abstract: "(5 $\leq$ \[HCN\]/\[HCO$^+$\] $\leq$ 20: non-LTE analysis)"]
- result: Non-LTE n_H2 and T_kin ranges (high-J) = 10^4.5–10^6 cm^-3; 70–550 K ± not stated cm^-3; K [abstract: "dense (10$^{4.5}$ cm$^{-3}$ $\leq$ $n_{\rm{H_2}}$ $\leq$ 10$^6$ cm$^{-3}$), hot (70 K $\leq$ $T_{\rm{kin}}$ $\leq$ 550 K) regions"]
- limitation (authors): Dynamical mass is simple Keplerian estimate and lower limit [6 Dense molecular gas kinematics: "Note that the estimation we present in this section is based on the simple assumptions of Keplerian rotation."]
- limitation (authors): Submm-HCN diagram is tentative, few samples [7.2 Molecular line diagnostics: "this is a tentative view as we do not have clear theoretical evidence to support the use of this diagram, and it is based on few samples"]
