  - method: Correlation plots of column densities (HNC-HCO+, HCN-HNC, CN-HCN, CN-HNC, hydrocarbons, CO-HCO+, HCO-H13CO+, CS-SO, CS-SiO) with literature data overlaid; N(HCO+) used as N(H2) proxy; isotopologue ratios from column densities or opacity li… [3.6 Chemical compositions: "In the following subsections, the column density of HCO$^+$, $N$(HCO$^+$), is used as an indicator of $N$(H$_2$) because we cannot directly measure it for individual Galactic disk clouds"]
