### 2017ApJ...850..170O: High Dense Gas Fraction in Intensely Star-forming Dusty Galaxies (2017; high_z_galaxies; observational_alma_primary)
- question: Do lensed high-z dusty starbursts (SDP.9, SDP.11) have dense gas excitation, line ratios and L_IR-L_dense relations like local (U)LIRGs, and is their dense gas fraction higher?
- step 3: Measure line fluxes
  - method: Velocity-integrated fluxes from zero-moment maps; 3 sigma upper limits [4.3: "All velocity-integrated line fluxes have been calculated from the zero-moment maps."]
  - assumption: HNC(3-2) upper limit in SDP.11 assumes same width as CO and no velocity offset [4.3: "we have assumed that its width is the same as the detected CO line and there is no velocity offset"]
- step 4: Non-LTE modelling of CO SLED and CO+HCN SLEDs
  - method: Grid of Myradex LVG models, likelihood marginalised over parameters [4.2: "We marginalize the parameters by integrating the likelihood distribution over all other parameters."]
  - software: Myradex
  - parameter: n_H2 = 1e2-1e8 cm^-3; Tkin = 10^0.5-10^3 K; dv/dr = 1-1e3 km/s/pc [4.2: "number density of molecular hydrogen $n_{\rm H_2} = 10^2$ – $10^8$ cm$^{-3}$, kinetic temperature $T_{\rm kin} = 10^{0.5} - 10^3 \, {\rm K}$"]
  - assumption: CO abundance 1e-4, T_CMB=7.004 K, HCN abundance 2e-8, single component [4.2: "We adopt a CO abundance relative to H$_2$ of $10^{-4}$."] [4.3: "We keep the HCN abundance (relative to ${\rm H_2}$) to be 2$\times 10^{-8}$"]
  - fitting: Likelihood grid, marginalisation [4.2: "we calculate the likelihood distributions for all parameter combinations following (cite: Ward2003ApJ...587..171W)"]
  - validation: Consistency of Tkin and column density between CO-only and CO+HCN fits [4.3: "We see that the $T_{\rm kin}$ and column density are consistent with the CO-based results."]
- step 5: Dense gas mass, depletion time and line ratios
  - method: Demagnified L_IR and line luminosities compared to literature; M_dense from L'_HCN(1-0) [4.7: "$M_{\rm dense} \sim 8.4 \times 10^{10} \, M_\odot$"]
  - assumption: M_dense = 10 L'_HCN(1-0) [4.7: "Assuming the relation between the dense molecular gas mass and the HCN(1–0) luminosity $M_{\rm dense} \sim 10 \times L'_{\rm HCN(1-0)}"]
  - validation: Compared with local galaxies and PDR/XDR models [Results and discussion, The HCN/HNC rat…: "According to the models of (cite: Meijerink2007A&A...461..793M), the high HCN(1–0)/HNC(1–0) ratios found for SDP.9 and SDP.11 could be only explained by PDR dominated regions"]
- result: HCN(3-2) flux SDP.9 = 0.66 ± 0.11 Jy km/s [Table 1: "| HCN(3–2) \[${\rm Jy} \, {\rm km} \, {\rm s}^{-1}$\] | $0.66 \pm 0.11$ | $0.54 \pm 0.08$ |"]
- result: HCN(3-2) flux SDP.11 = 0.54 ± 0.08 Jy km/s [Table 1: "| HCN(3–2) \[${\rm Jy} \, {\rm km} \, {\rm s}^{-1}$\] | $0.66 \pm 0.11$ | $0.54 \pm 0.08$ |"]
- result: HCN(1-0) flux SDP.9 = 0.17 ± 0.06 Jy km/s [Table 1: "| HCN(1–0) \[${\rm Jy} \, {\rm km} \, {\rm s}^{-1}$\] | $0.17 \pm 0.06$ | – |"]
- result: CO SLED best-fit n(H2) = 3.2e5 ± not stated cm^-3 [4.2: "$n(\rm H_2) = 3.2 \times 10^{5} \, {\rm cm^{-3}}$"]
- result: CO SLED M_H2 SDP.9 = 1.3e11 ± not stated Msun [4.2: "$M_{\rm H_2} = 1.3 \times 10^{11} \, M_\odot$"]
- result: M_dense SDP.9 = 8.4e10 ± not stated Msun [4.7: "we obtain $M_{\rm dense} \sim 8.4 \times 10^{10} \, M_\odot$"]
- result: L'HCN(1-0)/L'CO(1-0) SDP.9 = ~0.37 ± not stated dimensionless [4.7: "The $L'_{\rm HCN(1-0)} / L'_{\rm CO(1-0)} \sim 0.37$ found for SDP.9"]
- result: Dense gas depletion time SDP.9 = ~40 ± not stated Myr [4.5: "implying a dense gas depletion time of $\tau_{\rm dep} \sim 40 \, {\rm Myr}$"]
- limitation (authors): Differential magnification is a main uncertainty [3 Lens modelling: "The possible differential magnification between different transitions represents one of the main sources of uncertainty in the analysis presented in this work."]
- limitation (authors): Scatter and lack of homogeneous high-z samples prevent redshift trends [abstract: "prevents us from distinguishing differential trends with redshift"]
- not stated (card): ALMA CASA version and calibrators; Line-free channels and moment-map velocity ranges; Image size and cell size; uvmcmcfit priors and run settings; Myradex grid sampling and priors; Uncertainty derivation for line fluxes; Conversion of L' used for CO(1-0) and HCN luminosities, incl. L_IR demagnification details

### 2013A&A...555A.112P: Global collapse of molecular clouds as a formation mechanism for the most massive stars (2013; star_formation, milky_way_ism; observational_alma_primary)
- question: Does the kinematics of the dense gas in the IRDC SDC335 indicate global collapse that builds up massive cores, as opposed to primordial fragmentation?
- step 3: Core systemic velocities and filament velocities
  - method: Gaussian fits to CH3OH spectra; N2H+ hyperfine fitting [4.1: "Gaussian fits to the methanol spectra observed at the central position of the two cores"]
  - software: GILDAS
  - fitting: Hyperfine fitting in GILDAS [4.3 ALMA N2H+(1-0) cloud velocity field: "the N$_2$H$^+$(1-0) hyperfine line-fitting (performed with GILDAS) gives an opacity lower than 1 everywhere in the cloud"]
- step 4: HCO+ abundance via RADEX
  - method: Iterate column density to match observed Tpeak [4.2: "Then we iterate on the last input parameter, i.e. the molecule column density"]
  - software: RADEX
  - assumption: Tkin 20+-5 K, density 6e4 cm-3, dispersion 1.3 km/s [4.2: "the kinetic temperature ($20\pm5$ K, estimated from *Herschel* data)"]
  - validation: [HCO+]/[H13CO+] compared with expected 12C/13C [4.2 Mopra HCO+(1-0) self-absorbed lines: "the predicted $\rm{[^{12}C]/[^{13}C]}$ is around 30 (cite: langer1993; savage2002). The value we find is about half this value, which, considering the uncertainties on these kinds of measurements, is in reasonable agreement."]
- step 5: Infall velocity via RATRAN
  - method: Grid of 1D models varying infall velocity and dispersion, compared by reduced chi2 [5.3: "For each spectrum we calculated a reduced $\chi^2$ parameter representative of the quality of the fit."]
  - software: RATRAN
  - parameter: rho∝r^-1.5, T=20 K, X(HCO+)=7e-10, [HCO+]/[H13CO+]=30 [5.3: "a cloud-density profile $\rho\propto r^{-1.5}$, and a constant temperature profile of 20 K"]
  - fitting: grid, reduced chi2 [5.3 Collapse on large scales: "We then ran a grid of models varying the last two input parameters, i.e., the infall velocity and the velocity dispersion."]
  - validation: H13CO+ predictions compared in Appendix B [5.3 Collapse on large scales: "The corresponding H$^{13}$CO$^+$(1-0) predictions from the model are displayed in Appendix B."]
- result: Infall velocity = 0.7 ± 0.2 km/s [abstract: "$V_{inf} =0.7(\pm0.2)$ km/s"]
- result: HCO+ abundance = 7e-10 ± +8/-4 e-10 dimensionless [4.2: "$X_{HCO^+}=7^{+8}_{-4}\times10^{-10}$"]
- limitation (authors): Dust opacity, temperature uncertainties; 1D model cannot describe filaments [5.3: "Obviously, a 1D model cannot describe the detailed kinematics of the filamentary structures observed in SDC335"]
- not stated (card): CASA version and calibration/imaging parameters (weighting, cleaning, masks); Line-free channels and continuum subtraction method; Combination parameters for Mopra and ALMA short spacing in GILDAS; Mopra data reduction details; RATRAN grid details and fit criteria for infall velocity; Herschel colour-temperature conversion from 160/350 ratio; Details of ALMA fit regions for N2H+ hyperfine fits

### 2019ApJ...883..193N: The ALMA Discovery of the Rotating Disk and Fast Outflow of Cold Molecular Gas in NGC 1275 (2019; agn_and_quasars, nearby_galaxies, galaxy_clusters_and_sz; observational_alma_primary)
- question: What are the morphology and kinematics of the cold molecular gas in the inner kpc to ~30 pc of NGC 1275, how is the AGN fed, what do the blue-shifted absorption features imply, and what is the SMBH mass from gas dynamics?
- step 5: Absorption optical depth and column density
  - method: tau from 40 mJy absorption against 7 Jy continuum; LTE, covering factor 1, Tex 100 K, HCN/H2 = 1e-9 [3.2 The HCN(3-2) and HCO+(3-2) Lines: "Under the assumption of the local thermodynamic equilibrium and a covering factor of 1, we obtain the H$_{2}$ column density of $2.3\times10^{22}$ cm$^{-2}$."]
  - assumption: HCN-H2 abundance 1e-9 [3.2 The HCN(3-2) and HCO+(3-2) Lines: "Here we assume a HCN-H$_{2}$ abundance ratio of $10^{-9}$ (cite: Smith2014)."]
  - validation: spectra on continuum-unsubtracted images and archival data [3.2 The HCN(3-2) and HCO+(3-2) Lines: "To check that these features are not an artifact caused by the process of continuum subtraction, we also show the spectrum measured on the continuum unsubtracted images"]
- result: H2 column density of absorber = 2.3e22 ± not stated cm^-2 [3.2 The HCN(3-2) and HCO+(3-2) Lines: "we obtain the H$_{2}$ column density of $2.3\times10^{22}$ cm$^{-2}$"]
- result: Absorption optical depth = 0.0057 ± not stated dimensionless [3.2 The HCN(3-2) and HCO+(3-2) Lines: "yielding the optical depth of 0.0057"]
- limitation (authors): Missing flux from lack of short baselines, so masses are lower limits [4.1 Filaments: "Note that the estimated mass should be a lower limit since the total emissions cannot be recovered because of the lack of short interferometric baselines."]
