- step 2: Form pure emission spectra of HCO+, 12CO, and 13CO from IRAM 30m observations
  - method: Average four HCO+ emission spectra displaced by 1.2 HPBW (30'') in the four cardinal directions from the continuum source to avoid absorption contamination; average five positions (on-source and four displaced by 1 HPBW = 22'') for 12CO an… [2.2. Emission line spectra: "The HCO+ profiles we show are averages of spectra displaced by 1.2 HPBW = 30'' from the continuum source in each of the four cardinal directions, as discussed in Section F."] [Appendix F: Forming emission spectra in…: "The spectra toward and displaced 1 HPBW = 22'' from the continuum differ little so we averaged all five positions to form the 12CO and 13CO spectra shown in Figure 6."]
  - parameter: Channel spacing 48.8 kHz (0.164 km s^-1) and spectral resolution 97.7 kHz (0.33 km s^-1) at 89.1885 GHz [2.2. Emission line spectra: "The IRAM 30m emission profiles have a channel spacing and approximate spectral resolution of 48.8 and 97.7 kHz, or 0.164 and 0.33 km s^-1 at the HCO+ rest frequency."]
