- step 3: Analyze Galactic-scale distributions and power-law abundance relations across the sample
  - method: Perform power-law linear regressions in log-log space of E_B-V, N(HI), N(H2), and W_CO against sin(|b|), and of molecular column densities against E_B-V, N(HCO+), and N(C2H). [3.1. Galactic-scale properties: "The gas and dust column densities are plotted against sin(|b|), which is proportional to the nominal path length through a plane-parallel stratified Galactic disk. The numerical values derived from these plots are given in Table 1."] [Table 1 footnote: "a and b are fits to log (value of the y-species) = a+b×log (value of the x-species), and r is the correlation coefficient."]
