- step 4: Decompose HCO+, HCN, and C2H absorption profiles into Gaussian kinematic components
  - method: Simultaneously fit all kinematic and hyperfine components by varying central optical depth, central velocity, and FWHM to minimize deviations from the observed line/continuum ratio exp(-tau), using HCO+ decomposition as an initial template… [4. Component decomposition: "For each species, the decomposition simultaneously fit all kinematic components and hyperfine components by varying the central optical depth, central velocity, and profile FWHM while minimizing deviations from the observed line/continuum ratio exp(-tau)."] [4. Component decomposition: "We used the results for HCO+ as an initial template for HCN and C2H in decompositions that considered all observed kinematic and hyperfine components."]
  - parameter: Velocity matching criterion: separation in central velocity < 1/3 of the FWHM of the narrower component [4. Component decomposition: "The matched components are those for which the separation in central velocity is smaller than one-third of the FWHM of the narrower of the possible pair of components."]
