- result: Calculated binding energy of phenyl radical (C6H5) = 2056 ± not stated K [4.1. Hot Core Model: "As a result, we obtain binding energy (scaled by 1.416, because we use water monomer as a substrate here) of C 6 H 5 and C 6 H 5 OH as 2056 K and 5476 K, respectively."]
- result: Calculated binding energy of phenol (C6H5OH) = 5476 ± not stated K [4.1. Hot Core Model: "As a result, we obtain binding energy (scaled by 1.416, because we use water monomer as a substrate here) of C 6 H 5 and C 6 H 5 OH as 2056 K and 5476 K, respectively."]
