### 2020ApJ...902..140N: ALMA Observations of HCO<SUP>+</SUP> and HCN Emission in the Massive Star-forming Region N55 of the Large Magellanic Cloud (2020; star_formation, nearby_galaxies; observational_alma_primary)
- question: How do the properties of dense molecular clumps (size, linewidth, mass, dense gas fraction) relate to star formation in the quiescent N 55-S region of the LMC, compared with other LMC GMCs
- step 2: Make velocity-integrated intensity maps
  - method: Integrate HCO+ and HCN cubes along the velocity axis [HCO and HCN emission in N 55: "These maps are obtained by integrating the emission line data cubes along the velocity axis."]
- step 4: Derive HCO+ and H2 column density and optical depth
  - method: LTE analysis with peak optical depth from peak brightness temperature, then N_H2 from assumed HCO+ abundance [Clump column density: "We obtain the peak optical depth ($\tau_{\rm p}$) from the peak brightness temperature of each clump using the equation (cite: barnes2011)"]
  - parameter: Tex = 30 K [Clump column density: "We assume $T_{\rm ex}=30$ K as the excitation temperature of the HCO$^{+}$(1$-$0) clumps in the N 55-S for further calculations."]
  - parameter: Background temperature 2.72 K [Clump column density: "$T_{\rm bg}$ is the background temperature taken to be 2.72 K."]
  - parameter: Q_rot = 14.4 [Clump column density: "The partition function $Q_{rot}$ of HCO$^{+}$($1-0$) transition is 14.4 at $T_{\rm ex}=30$ K (cite: rohlfs2004; mangum2015)."]
  - assumption: HCO+/H2 abundance X = 1e-9 [Clump column density: "Assuming the relative abundance of HCO$^{+}$ to H$_{2}$ to be X=10$^{-9}$"]
  - assumption: Gaussian emission line profile [Clump column density: "we assume the emission line profiles, $\phi(V)$, to be Gaussian"]
  - validation: Tex sensitivity: 40 K lowers N_p by ~28%, 20 K raises it by ~39% [Clump column density: "For $T_{\rm ex}$ = 40 K, the $N_{\rm p}$ values of the clumps are $\sim$ 28% lower compared to the values derived for $T_{\rm ex}$ = 30 K and $\sim$ 39% higher for $T_{\rm ex}$ = 20 K."]
- step 6: Estimate dense gas fraction
  - method: CO-traced H2 mass (L_CO, X_CO, 30% missing-flux correction) compared with HCO+ mass sum [Dense gas fraction: "Thus the dense gas fraction in the N 55-S region is 0.025$\pm$0.005."]
  - parameter: X_CO = 2e20 cm-2 K-1 km-1 s [Dense gas fraction: "Hence we use $X_{\rm CO}$=2$\times$10$^{20}$ cm$^{-2}$ K$^{-1}$ km$^{-1}$ s in our calculation."]
