### 2018A&A...620A.115B: Dense-gas tracers and carbon isotopes in five 2.5 &lt; z &lt; 4 lensed dusty star-forming galaxies from the SPT SMG sample (2018; high_z_galaxies, astrochemistry; observational_alma_primary)
- question: How much dense, actively star-forming gas (HCN, HCO+, HNC 5-4) and which 13CO/12CO isotopic ratios do lensed SPT dusty star-forming galaxies at 2.5<z<4 show, and how do they compare with local galaxies?
- step 5: Deblend HNC(5-4) and CN(4-3)
  - method: Joint fit with common width and velocity offset and positivity prior on both, then mean ratio [2.6: "We fitted simultaneously all the lines in the spectrum including HNC(5-4) and CN(4-3) and forced all the lines to have the same width and velocity offset"]
  - validation: Simulation recovers blended ratios [9: "The ratios including blended lines are also well recovered."]
- step 6: Compare with local LIR-L'HCN relation and line ratios
  - method: Convert 5-4 to 4-3 with Mills2013 ratios, correct for magnification, compare with Zhang2014 relation, HCO+/HCN, HNC/HCN, HCN/[CI], HCN/CO, 12CO/13CO [3.1: "We also corrected our sources for the magnification based on (cite: Spilker2016)."]
  - assumption: Local 5-4/4-3 ratio applies; differential lensing negligible; Planck2015 cosmology, Chabrier IMF [4.3: "We thus neglected this effect in this paper."]
  - validation: Sample variance 0.28/sqrt(5)=0.125 dex considered [3.1: "we thus expect a 1-$\sigma$ sample variance for five objects of 0.28 / $\sqrt{5}$ = 0.125 dex"]
- result: HCN deficit relative to Zhang2014 = factor 1.6 (0.20 dex); 2.0 (0.30 dex) after LIR homogenization ± ~2 sigma dimensionless [3.1: "This corresponds to a deficit by a factor of 1.6 (0.20 dex) corresponding to a 2.5 $\sigma$ difference."]
- result: Mean HNC(5-4)/HCN(5-4) flux ratio = 1.03 ± +0.59/-0.39 dimensionless [3.3: "found a ratio compatible with unity (1.03$_{-0.39}^{+0.59}$)"]
- result: Mean HNC(5-4)/CN(4-3) ratio = 1.60 ± +1.74/-0.82 dimensionless [2.6: "We found a mean HNC(5-4)/CN(4-3) ratio of 1.60$_{-0.82}^{+1.74}$."]
- limitation (authors): Low S/N; conversion 5-4 to 4-3 uncertain; differential lensing neglected [3.1: "It is therefore not possible to draw any firm conclusions, especially considering the uncertainties involved in converting our HCN(5-4) fluxes to HCN(4-3)."]
- not stated (card): Cell size, image size and clean mask details; Rest frequencies used for lines; Exact flagging list beyond DA48; CASA version; Bootstrap fitting code (not released); fitting optimizer and starting values; LIR values and uncertainties source tables per source beyond Table 2; Details of the magnification handling for luminosity conversion

